# nvfbc-relay policy replay fixture
# Get Medieval (KCD), 78 min of real streamed gameplay, b:vsync on the defaults (source rate not declared, 60 assumed; comb lock, 75 ms extra lag, flip timing and dejitter on) with capture through Windows.Graphics.Capture (-wgc), the mouse pointer in the picture and the frames that change less than a tenth of the largest area changed in the last half second left out, the frame pool on a device of its own and its textures opened on the present's device, and a frame shown as it is presented through the GPU's copy engine, 2026-10-23, build d2cb213; cut to the stretch the stream's video shows, 50.3 s to 4707.6 s
# units: microseconds. first value absolute, rest are deltas.
description Get Medieval (KCD), 78 min of real streamed gameplay, b:vsync on the defaults (source rate not declared, 60 assumed; comb lock, 75 ms extra lag, flip timing and dejitter on) with capture through Windows.Graphics.Capture (-wgc), the mouse pointer in the picture and the frames that change less than a tenth of the largest area changed in the last half second left out, the frame pool on a device of its own and its textures opened on the present's device, and a frame shown as it is presented through the GPU's copy engine, 2026-10-23, build d2cb213; cut to the stretch the stream's video shows, 50.3 s to 4707.6 s
# What the RELAY did on this capture. The replay model is only trustworthy
# for a configuration where it reproduces these; the test checks that.
field_worst_run 31
field_long_runs 0
field_synth_pct 0.8
field_pull_wraps 93
# WHAT IT COVERS: the 2026-10-23 stream, 77.6 minutes cut to the gameplay its video shows,
# captured as the 2026-10-22 second stream was (Windows.Graphics.Capture, the mouse pointer in
# the picture, the small-change frames left out, the pool on a device of its own) and presented
# through the GPU's copy engine: 283366 of the log's 286737 presents were copied there, 3371
# drawn, none failed. The policy is the one the tree ships. The game hitched (20 to 100 ms) 455
# times (352 an hour) and stalled for 100 ms or more 106 times (82 an hour), in 111 bursts, 67 of
# them with a stall, and with no periodic stretch. The lock released 7 times, in the field and on
# the replay at the same moments: 1359.15, 1731.23, 1921.10, 4119.36, 4470.24, 4659.64 and
# 4678.89 s. Six of them fall inside a hitch burst or within 0.4 s after one; the one at 1731.23 s
# has no hitch in the 29 s before it. The worst blend run, 31 presents in the field and on the
# replay, starts at the 1921.10 s release, just after a burst of 9 hitches and a 144 ms stall
# that ends at 1921.0 s. Of the 53 moves on the replay, 7 land more than 2 ms from a real frame.
# WINDOW. The video pairs with this log at log time = video time + 50.287 s, from the 2427
# marked frames in its first 40 s, within 0.42 ms of that offset (p90). The video runs 4657.3 s
# with no holes, opens on gameplay indoors and ends on gameplay after the sleep wheel and the
# inventory, so the cut is the whole video, 50.3 s to 4707.6 s of log time, and the marked frames
# lie inside it. Every second inside the cut that falls out of the 60 fps regime is a hitch
# second, 26 of them in 26 runs, none longer than 2 s, so nothing was removed from the middle.
# FIDELITY. The capture ran the policy the tree ships, so the two lines are comparable. The
# replay line (the plain arm) reads synth 0.7% against 0.8%, worst run 31 against 31, runs >= 50
# 0 against 0 and pull wraps 93 against 93. On the dejitter arm, which is how the stream ran and
# what the counts here use, blends are 2271 against 2262, repeats 689 against 685, skips 233
# against 234, pull wraps 93 against 93 and the worst run 31 against 31, all inside the corpus's
# fidelity limits. The replay makes 53 moves, 18 of them late, and the field's log has 55 in the
# window.
# Bounds on the REPLAY (not the field): inequalities, so an improvement passes and only a
# regression fails. Measured on the policy the capture ran.
max_worst_run 31
max_long_runs 0
max_synth_pct 1.1
min_reseeds 129
max_pull_wraps 93
extra_lag_ms 75
arrivals 555602
